        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "48a03bd6-c8b2-5a86-9fbb-d54576571fba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Catasetum, Lomandra\n- Taxonomy: Orchidaceae, Epidendroideae, Cymbidieae, Catasetinae, Asparagaceae, Lomandroideae\n- Horticulture: horticultural trade\n\nFacts:\n- Catasetum is abbreviated as Ctsm in the horticultural trade.\n- Catasetum is a genus of showy epiphytic orchids in the family Orchidaceae, subfamily Epidendroideae, tribe Cymbidieae, and subtribe Catasetinae.\n- Catasetum includes 166 species, many of which are highly prized in horticulture.\n- Lomandra, also known as mat rushes, is a genus of perennial herbs in the family Asparagaceae and subfamily Lomandroideae.",
